-- title:
--   Existence of a Néron identity component for J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   For every prime $p$, the type `JZeroNeronIdentityComponent p` is inhabited. Unfolding the structure, this asserts the existence of a scheme $G$ (in the zeroth universe) with a morphism $g : G \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ carrying a relative group law $L$ over $\mathbf Z$, i.e. for every $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ a group structure (multiplication, unit, inverse, associativity, unit and inverse laws) on the set $\{\varphi : T \to G \mid \varphi \circ g = t\}$ of $T$-points over $\mathbf Z$, compatible with precomposition $T' \to T$, and commutative; together with a bijection `pts` from $J_0(p)$, taken to be the degree-zero Picard group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$, onto the $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-points of $g$. The data are required to satisfy: $g$ is smooth, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact and surjective, with topologically preconnected fibres; `pts` is additive and equivariant for $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbf Q}/\mathbf Q)$, the Galois action corresponding to precomposition with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\sigma$; every element of $\mathrm{HeckeAlg} = \mathbf Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ acting through `heckeModuleBar p` is induced by an $L$-additive endomorphism of $G$ over $\mathbf Z$; multiplication by $n$ on $G$ is flat and surjective for $n > 0$; the subgroup generated by the $\mathbf Z$-sections of $g$ has finite index in the Galois-fixed subgroup of $J_0(p)$; and the structure's remaining requirements, summarised here.
--
--   This is the existence statement for the identity component of the Néron model of $J_0(p)$ over $\mathbf Z$, packaged as a smooth commutative group scheme over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ with connected fibres whose $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-points recover $J_0(p)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$ together with its Galois and Hecke actions. It is the geometric input for the construction of the Néron core of the $q$-primary torsion of $J_0(p)$, used by [`ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionCore_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronPrimaryTorsionCore_of_dvd).
